* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
# .sql is pinned for a reason beyond tidiness: a migration file's body must md5-match
# `schema_migrations.statements`, and that hash is over LF bytes. Without this line
# `* text=auto` plus core.autocrlf=true checks .sql out as CRLF on Windows, and the check
# that proves a recorded migration is the one that ran fails for every file at once.
*.sql text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf